MCSKIP MT,<>
MCINS %.
The macros that clear the environment take out the local
constructions and leave the global ones.
MCDEFG KEEP AS <survivor>
MCDEF DROP AS <casualty>
KEEP and DROP before
MCNODEF
KEEP and DROP after
Note the blank line above: these macros do not have a newline as a
closing delimiter, so the newline that follows a call of one reaches
the output like any other character.
A name can be defined again once it has gone, and the definition has
to be bracketed or it would be replaced by its own value first.
MCDEF <DROP> AS <replacement>
DROP at the end
